{"id":"7a9cfbd003ad8ae1","group":"58","path":"58/batch03/58-thm-continuum-function.md","title":"Continuum Function Theorem","display":"thm-continuum-function — Continuum Function Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-continuum-function","aliases":["58-thm-continuum-function"],"display":"thm-continuum-function — Continuum Function Theorem","depends_on":["[[58-thm-easton]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-continuum-function"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-continuum-function</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-continuum-function — Continuum Function Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"62a46f3922b57bd0\" href=\"?note=62a46f3922b57bd0\" title=\"58-thm-easton\">58-thm-easton</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbf V,\\mathbf W\">\\(\\mathbf V,\\mathbf W\\)</span> are proper-class universes and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F,\\mathbb P,G\">\\(F,\\mathbb P,G\\)</span> are class parameters in the ambient class metatheory</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZFC}\">\\(\\mathrm{ZFC}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{GCH}\">\\(\\mathrm{GCH}\\)</span> denote the usual theory and generalized-continuum schema</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{DefinableEastonFunction}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(F,\\mathbf V)\">\\(\\mathrm{DefinableEastonFunction}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(F,\\mathbf V)\\)</span> is the sourced predicate requiring a definable amenable, cardinal-valued, monotone function on the infinite regular cardinals, with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa&lt;\\operatorname{cf}^{\\mathbf V}(F(\\kappa))\">\\(\\kappa&lt;\\operatorname{cf}^{\\mathbf V}(F(\\kappa))\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{EastonClassForcingExtension}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(\\mathbf W,\\mathbf V,\\mathbb P,G)\">\\(\\mathrm{EastonClassForcingExtension}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(\\mathbf W,\\mathbf V,\\mathbb P,G)\\)</span> is the tame Easton-support class-forcing extension predicate from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"62a46f3922b57bd0\" href=\"?note=62a46f3922b57bd0\" title=\"58-thm-easton\">58-thm-easton</a></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\models_{\\mathrm{Cls}}\">\\(\\models_{\\mathrm{Cls}}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\exists_{\\mathrm{Cls}}\">\\(\\exists_{\\mathrm{Cls}}\\)</span> are class-metatheoretic satisfaction and quantification</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}continuum\\text{-}function}\\vdash_{\\mathrm{meta}}{}&amp;\n(\\mathbf V,\\in)\\models_{\\mathrm{Cls}}\\bigl(\\mathrm{ZFC}\\mathbin{+}\\mathrm{GCH}\\bigr)\n\\land\\mathrm{DefinableEastonFunction}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(F,\\mathbf V)\\\\\n\\to{}&amp;\\exists_{\\mathrm{Cls}}\\mathbf W,\\mathbb P,G\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{EastonClassForcingExtension}_{\\mathrm{meta}}\n(\\mathbf W,\\mathbf V,\\mathbb P,G)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land(\\mathbf W,\\in)\\models_{\\mathrm{Cls}}\\mathrm{ZFC}\n\\land\\operatorname{Card}^{\\mathbf W}=\\operatorname{Card}^{\\mathbf V}\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land\\forall\\alpha\\in\\operatorname{Ord}^{\\mathbf V}\\;\n\\bigl(\\operatorname{cf}^{\\mathbf W}(\\alpha)=\\operatorname{cf}^{\\mathbf V}(\\alpha)\\bigr)\n\\land\\forall\\kappa\\in\\operatorname{Reg}^{\\mathbf V}\\;\n\\bigl((2^\\kappa)^{\\mathbf W}=F(\\kappa)\\bigr)\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}continuum\\text{-}function}\\vdash_{\\mathrm{meta}}{}&amp;\n(\\mathbf V,\\in)\\models_{\\mathrm{Cls}}\\bigl(\\mathrm{ZFC}\\mathbin{+}\\mathrm{GCH}\\bigr)\n\\land\\mathrm{DefinableEastonFunction}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(F,\\mathbf V)\\\\\n\\to{}&amp;\\exists_{\\mathrm{Cls}}\\mathbf W,\\mathbb P,G\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{EastonClassForcingExtension}_{\\mathrm{meta}}\n(\\mathbf W,\\mathbf V,\\mathbb P,G)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land(\\mathbf W,\\in)\\models_{\\mathrm{Cls}}\\mathrm{ZFC}\n\\land\\operatorname{Card}^{\\mathbf W}=\\operatorname{Card}^{\\mathbf V}\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land\\forall\\alpha\\in\\operatorname{Ord}^{\\mathbf V}\\;\n\\bigl(\\operatorname{cf}^{\\mathbf W}(\\alpha)=\\operatorname{cf}^{\\mathbf V}(\\alpha)\\bigr)\n\\land\\forall\\kappa\\in\\operatorname{Reg}^{\\mathbf V}\\;\n\\bigl((2^\\kappa)^{\\mathbf W}=F(\\kappa)\\bigr)\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This is the continuum-function formulation of Easton's theorem.  Its domain is the proper class of regular cardinals, so the forcing, function, universes, and satisfaction claims are explicitly class-metatheoretic.</li>\n<li>The former hybrid statement treated a set <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M\">\\(M\\)</span> as a structure without selecting satisfaction, passed metatheoretic cardinal predicates as formulas, and called a six-place set relation a full class-forcing theorem.  Those object/meta mismatches are removed.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-thm-easton","status":"resolved","id":"62a46f3922b57bd0","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-thm-easton]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-thm-easton","status":"resolved","id":"62a46f3922b57bd0","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{EastonClassForcingExtension}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(\\mathbf W,\\mathbf V,\\mathbb P,G)$ is the tame Easton-support class-forcing extension predicate from [[58-thm-easton]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathbf V,\\mathbf W","display":false},{"tex":"F,\\mathbb P,G","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ZFC}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{GCH}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{DefinableEastonFunction}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(F,\\mathbf V)","display":false},{"tex":"\\kappa<\\operatorname{cf}^{\\mathbf V}(F(\\kappa))","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{EastonClassForcingExtension}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(\\mathbf W,\\mathbf V,\\mathbb P,G)","display":false},{"tex":"\\models_{\\mathrm{Cls}}","display":false},{"tex":"\\exists_{\\mathrm{Cls}}","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}continuum\\text{-}function}\\vdash_{\\mathrm{meta}}{}&\n(\\mathbf V,\\in)\\models_{\\mathrm{Cls}}\\bigl(\\mathrm{ZFC}\\mathbin{+}\\mathrm{GCH}\\bigr)\n\\land\\mathrm{DefinableEastonFunction}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(F,\\mathbf V)\\\\\n\\to{}&\\exists_{\\mathrm{Cls}}\\mathbf W,\\mathbb P,G\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{EastonClassForcingExtension}_{\\mathrm{meta}}\n(\\mathbf W,\\mathbf V,\\mathbb P,G)\\\\\n&\\quad\\land(\\mathbf W,\\in)\\models_{\\mathrm{Cls}}\\mathrm{ZFC}\n\\land\\operatorname{Card}^{\\mathbf W}=\\operatorname{Card}^{\\mathbf V}\\\\\n&\\quad\\land\\forall\\alpha\\in\\operatorname{Ord}^{\\mathbf V}\\;\n\\bigl(\\operatorname{cf}^{\\mathbf W}(\\alpha)=\\operatorname{cf}^{\\mathbf V}(\\alpha)\\bigr)\n\\land\\forall\\kappa\\in\\operatorname{Reg}^{\\mathbf V}\\;\n\\bigl((2^\\kappa)^{\\mathbf W}=F(\\kappa)\\bigr)\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"M","display":false}],"bytes":2375,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4097","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch03/58-thm-continuum-function.md|58-thm-continuum-function]]（batch03）"}],"outgoing":["62a46f3922b57bd0"]}